WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.720
AI governance should define where human judgment is required.

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:11.540
Some AI outputs may only support a user, while others may influence decisions that affect people, systems, or business processes.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:18.080
Human oversight is especially important when outcomes are sensitive, irreversible, high-impact, or difficult to appeal.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:19.980
Oversight should be meaningful.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:27.640
Reviewers need enough context, authority, training, and time to challenge or reject AI-assisted recommendations when appropriate.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:34.020
Accountability means people and teams remain responsible for decisions, even when AI tools assist the process.
